  "baselineControl": "exec-baseline.ts is the baseline exec.ts with only its child-process helper import rebased to the unchanged production helper; no other baseline source edits.",
  "driverSourceSha256": "69902248da5c64ddb66dfbb2ab911574f9ee16ca340748be189656f895120c11",
  "method": "Five serial baseline/candidate pairs, Node26 only. Real execCommand and waitForChildProcess; deterministic EventEmitter/PassThrough spawn-boundary fixture with prebuilt buffers. 4 warmups, 16 sampled invocations per fixture; separate CPU/timing pass delivers 256MiB total per fixture. Inspector samplingInterval=1024 includes objects collected by major/minor GC. No real subprocess startup is included in these throughput metrics.",
  "limits": [
    "Node/fixture/inspector allocations are included; samples are estimates. No constant speedup claim is made.",
    "Small wall-time p95 regressions are recorded: 256KiB/+5.86%,512KiB/+16.81% in these runs; absolute increases 7.6us and 23.4us. Windows CPU accounting is coarse.",
    "The baseline ignores maxBuffer: the capped comparison demonstrates stopped decoding, not identical accepted output.",
    "heapBefore/peakHeap/heapAfterGC are process heap observations at invocation boundaries, not proof of exact retained string bytes. WeakRef and listener/timer counts establish release independently.",
    "Input buffers are prebuilt and decoding builds required output strings; no raw chunk array/full-history scan/application full-output copy is introduced. V8 may flatten cons strings outside this fixture; no zero-V8-copy claim.",
    "T05-A owns direct child/reading ends only. Windows Job/POSIX group descendants belong to the separately planned T05-B."
  ],
